1497
01:42:43,490 --> 01:42:47,102
We know e-bikes and scooters are becoming more and more popular in our communities,

1498
01:42:47,215 --> 01:42:50,988
especially with our kids. Unfortunately, we're seeing a significant

1499
01:42:51,488 --> 01:42:55,211
increase in the number of injuries with riding e-bikes and scooters.

1500
01:42:56,046 --> 01:42:59,145
We want to get your attention. E-bikes and e-scooters

1501
01:42:59,241 --> 01:43:01,232
are not toys. They are vehicles.

1502
01:43:02,549 --> 01:43:06,129
Here at Unified Fire Authority, we want to make sure that everybody understands

1503
01:43:06,145 --> 01:43:09,517
the risks of riding, knows how to ride safely, and has the

1504
01:43:10,017 --> 01:43:12,536
proper safety equipment and wears it every time they ride.

1505
01:43:13,949 --> 01:43:17,128
Riding a traditional bike requires physical effort to build speed.

1506
01:43:17,626 --> 01:43:21,223
E-bikes and e-scooters are different. They provide a lot more power

1507
01:43:21,560 --> 01:43:25,060
with little to no effort, making it easier to reach higher

1508
01:43:25,108 --> 01:43:28,833
speeds. That combination of speed and minimal

1509
01:43:28,962 --> 01:43:32,253
effort can make it harder to recognize how much risk you're

1510
01:43:32,753 --> 01:43:36,783
taking and how quickly things can change. More speed means less

1511
01:43:36,831 --> 01:43:40,655
time to react, which can lead to very serious injuries,

1512
01:43:41,025 --> 01:43:44,784
especially when not wearing a helmet. In 2025

1513
01:43:45,284 --> 01:43:50,087
alone, Intermountain Healthcare emergency rooms across Utah treated 536

1514
01:43:50,587 --> 01:43:54,136
people for e-bike and e-scooter injuries. Furthermore, only about

1515
01:43:54,264 --> 01:43:57,494
40% of bike trauma patients were wearing a helmet at

1516
01:43:57,994 --> 01:44:02,056
the time of their crash. A new state law is now in effect requiring e-bike

1517
01:44:02,556 --> 01:44:06,648
and e-scooter riders under 21 to wear an approved helmet when riding on public

1518
01:44:06,713 --> 01:44:10,165
roads. Ideally, a full-face helmet, which offers the most

1519
01:44:10,665 --> 01:44:14,259
protection. These statistics are concerning, but there are steps

1520
01:44:14,759 --> 01:44:17,278
we can take to avoid many of these accidents and injuries.

1521
01:44:17,888 --> 01:44:21,164
So, what can we do about it?

1522
01:44:21,469 --> 01:44:25,210
Parents, pay close attention to the e-bikes and scooters your child

1523
01:44:25,258 --> 01:44:27,876
is riding. Make sure it's appropriate for their age.

1524
01:44:28,712 --> 01:44:31,154
Helmet on every ride, every time,

1525
01:44:31,765 --> 01:44:35,879
no exception. Teach your kids to follow traffic laws and signs,

1526
01:44:36,264 --> 01:44:40,105
ride at a safe speed, and always stay alert to what's happening around

1527
01:44:40,605 --> 01:44:44,186
them. At intersections and crosswalks, teach them to yield to

1528
01:44:44,202 --> 01:44:47,159
drivers and pedestrians, never blow through an intersection,

1529
01:44:47,416 --> 01:44:50,823
and make sure both parties can see each other before proceeding.

1530
01:44:51,980 --> 01:44:55,592
Make sure they're wearing visible clothing and have proper lights, especially in

1531
01:44:55,705 --> 01:44:59,398
low-light conditions. These simple steps can help

1532
01:44:59,898 --> 01:45:01,774
keep our kids safe every time they ride.

1533
01:45:02,930 --> 01:45:06,286
Remember, e-bikes and scooters are not toys. They are

1534
01:45:06,786 --> 01:45:09,979
vehicles. So let's all work together to make sure that our

1535
01:45:10,479 --> 01:45:11,858
kids make it home safely every time.

